./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0103.stderr.log:203:./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/documents/rec_003258_acl.docling.json:916:      "orig": "Tu et al., 2023). Recently, visual instruction tuning was introduced to open the possibility of a visual assistant in medicine (Li et al., 2023a; Lee et al., 2023). Additionally, there has been notable progress in extending the model's capabilities to handle biological sequences, including DNA sequences and chemical sequences represented by Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry Specification (SMILES) notation (Taylor et al., 2022; Consens et al., 2023; Zhang et al., 2024).",
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0103.stderr.log:204:./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/documents/rec_003258_acl.docling.json:917:      "text": "Tu et al., 2023). Recently, visual instruction tuning was introduced to open the possibility of a visual assistant in medicine (Li et al., 2023a; Lee et al., 2023). Additionally, there has been notable progress in extending the model's capabilities to handle biological sequences, including DNA sequences and chemical sequences represented by Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry Specification (SMILES) notation (Taylor et al., 2022; Consens et al., 2023; Zhang et al., 2024)."
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0103.stderr.log:274:./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:4:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 4, "text": "Tu et al., 2023). Recently, visual instruction tuning was introduced to open the possibility of a visual assistant in medicine (Li et al., 2023a; Lee et al., 2023). Additionally, there has been notable progress in extending the model's capabilities to handle biological sequences, including DNA sequences and chemical sequences represented by Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry Specification (SMILES) notation (Taylor et al., 2022; Consens et al., 2023; Zhang et al., 2024).\nDespite these advancements, multimodal research in biomedicine has focused on integrating text, image, and sequence data. While these modalities have proven invaluable in capturing certain medical nuances, they often overlook the structural intricacies inherent in biomedical graph data, such as knowledge graphs and protein structures. Consequently, the full potential of multimodal learning remains largely unexplored in addressing the multifaceted challenges encountered in computational biology and clinical research.", "contextualized_text": "Foundation Model for Biomedical Graphs: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Protein Structures to Large Language Models\n1 Introduction\nTu et al., 2023). Recently, visual instruction tuning was introduced to open the possibility of a visual assistant in medicine (Li et al., 2023a; Lee et al., 2023). Additionally, there has been notable progress in extending the model's capabilities to handle biological sequences, including DNA sequences and chemical sequences represented by Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry Specification (SMILES) notation (Taylor et al., 2022; Consens et al., 2023; Zhang et al., 2024).\nDespite these advancements, multimodal research in biomedicine has focused on integrating text, image, and sequence data. While these modalities have proven invaluable in capturing certain medical nuances, they often overlook the structural intricacies inherent in biomedical graph data, such as knowledge graphs and protein structures. Consequently, the full potential of multimodal learning remains largely unexplored in addressing the multifaceted challenges encountered in computational biology and clinical research.", "headings": ["Foundation Model for Biomedical Graphs: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Protein Structures to Large Language Models", "1 Introduction"], "pages": [1], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/8", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 1, "bbox": {"l": 305.80629020000003, "t": 621.1170782488575, "r": 526.2378946311701, "b": 486.0218583255826, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 477]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/9", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 1, "bbox": {"l": 306.14430710000005, "t": 485.4962975488576, "r": 526.238549209898, "b": 336.85140017558257, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 521]}]}], "headings": ["Foundation Model for Biomedical Graphs: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Protein Structures to Large Language Models", "1 Introduction"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 9293128959098327548, "filename": "rec_003258_acl.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0103.stderr.log:276:./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/markdown/rec_003258_acl.md:17:Tu et al., 2023). Recently, visual instruction tuning was introduced to open the possibility of a visual assistant in medicine (Li et al., 2023a; Lee et al., 2023). Additionally, there has been notable progress in extending the model's capabilities to handle biological sequences, including DNA sequences and chemical sequences represented by Simplified Molecular Input Line Entry Specification (SMILES) notation (Taylor et al., 2022; Consens et al., 2023; Zhang et al., 2024).
