./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:26:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 26, "text": "How do genes direct the production of proteins?\nMost genes contain the information needed to make functional molecules called proteins. ...", "contextualized_text": "3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation\nIntroduction to Genetics\nHow do genes direct the production of proteins?\nMost genes contain the information needed to make functional molecules called proteins. ...", "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "Introduction to Genetics"], "pages": [5], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/70", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 80.77803935000001, "t": 523.7572104988575, "r": 281.0234907119796, "b": 497.0614102755826, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 47]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/71", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 80.77803935000001, "t": 496.6568555488576, "r": 279.2169843403769, "b": 469.9610553255826, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 91]}]}], "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "Introduction to Genetics"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 9293128959098327548, "filename": "rec_003258_acl.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:27:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 27, "text": "Aloe is used topically (applied to the skin) and orally. Topical use of aloe is promoted for acne, ...\nTable 1: Examples of MedlinePlus pretrain data for each category.", "contextualized_text": "3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation\nDietary Supplements\nAloe is used topically (applied to the skin) and orally. Topical use of aloe is promoted for acne, ...\nTable 1: Examples of MedlinePlus pretrain data for each category.", "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "Dietary Supplements"], "pages": [5], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/73", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 80.38601975, "t": 455.21078334885755, "r": 279.39882631082094, "b": 414.9653056755826, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 102]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/74", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 70.54752785000001, "t": 404.44067897055754, "r": 289.30249120330757, "b": 380.4795479739076, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 65]}]}], "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "Dietary Supplements"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 9293128959098327548, "filename": "rec_003258_acl.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:28:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 28, "text": "MMLU(Massive Multitask Language Understanding) (Hendrycks et al., 2020) is a benchmark designed to measure the model's ability in knowledgeintensive QA across 57 subjects. These subjects cover various levels of education: high school, college, and professional level. Questions in the dataset are structured as four-way multiple choice questions (MCQs), offering a standardized format for evaluation. Within the extensive list of subjects, there are nine healthcare-related subjects which are college medicine, professional medicine, clinical knowledge, anatomy, high school biology, college biology, medical genetics, nutrition, and virology. Collectively, these nine subjects comprise a total of 1,871 questions in the test set.", "contextualized_text": "3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation\n3.2.1 MMLU_MED\nMMLU(Massive Multitask Language Understanding) (Hendrycks et al., 2020) is a benchmark designed to measure the model's ability in knowledgeintensive QA across 57 subjects. These subjects cover various levels of education: high school, college, and professional level. Questions in the dataset are structured as four-way multiple choice questions (MCQs), offering a standardized format for evaluation. Within the extensive list of subjects, there are nine healthcare-related subjects which are college medicine, professional medicine, clinical knowledge, anatomy, high school biology, college biology, medical genetics, nutrition, and virology. Collectively, these nine subjects comprise a total of 1,871 questions in the test set.", "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.1 MMLU_MED"], "pages": [5], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/76", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 70.8565433, "t": 335.7618111988576, "r": 291.0489176707652, "b": 132.91820402558255, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 730]}]}], "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.1 MMLU_MED"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 9293128959098327548, "filename": "rec_003258_acl.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:29:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 29, "text": "MedQA (Jin et al., 2021) is an open-ended MCQ dataset made from professional medical doctor license exams. The dataset is available in three ver-", "contextualized_text": "3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation\n3.2.2 MedQA\nMedQA (Jin et al., 2021) is an open-ended MCQ dataset made from professional medical doctor license exams. The dataset is available in three ver-", "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.2 MedQA"], "pages": [5], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/78", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 70.8565433, "t": 106.22133474885754, "r": 290.9448942013517, "b": 65.97585707558255, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 145]}]}], "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.2 MedQA"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 9293128959098327548, "filename": "rec_003258_acl.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:30:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 30, "text": "The following are multiple choice questions (with answers) about medqa.\nQuestion: A 67-year-old man with transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder comes to the physician because of a 2-day history of ringing sensation in his ear. He received this first course of neoadjuvant chemotherapy 1 week ago. Pure tone audiometry shows a sensorineural hearing loss of 45 dB. The expected beneficial effect of the drug that caused this patient's symptoms is most likely due to which of the following actions?\n- A. Inhibition of proteasome\n- B. Hyperstabilization of microtubules\n- C. Generation of free radicals\n- D. Cross-linking of DNA\nAnswer:", "contextualized_text": "3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation\n3.2.2 MedQA\nPrompt with Question\nThe following are multiple choice questions (with answers) about medqa.\nQuestion: A 67-year-old man with transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder comes to the physician because of a 2-day history of ringing sensation in his ear. He received this first course of neoadjuvant chemotherapy 1 week ago. Pure tone audiometry shows a sensorineural hearing loss of 45 dB. The expected beneficial effect of the drug that caused this patient's symptoms is most likely due to which of the following actions?\n- A. Inhibition of proteasome\n- B. Hyperstabilization of microtubules\n- C. Generation of free radicals\n- D. Cross-linking of DNA\nAnswer:", "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.2 MedQA", "Prompt with Question"], "pages": [5], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/80", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 315.70578515000005, "t": 757.2928866988575, "r": 514.5043629479185, "b": 730.5970864755826, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 71]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/81", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 316.06580315, "t": 730.1935317988576, "r": 516.3167093347074, "b": 595.0983118755826, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 427]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/82", "parent": {"cref": "#/groups/1"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "list_item", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 315.6727835000001, "t": 594.6947571988576, "r": 436.87894450505024, "b": 581.5486344255826, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 27]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/83", "parent": {"cref": "#/groups/1"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "list_item", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 316.06580315, "t": 581.1450797488576, "r": 480.69235306595033, "b": 567.9989569755826, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 37]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/84", "parent": {"cref": "#/groups/1"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "list_item", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 316.06580315, "t": 567.5944022488577, "r": 445.42146930993533, "b": 554.4482794755827, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 30]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/85", "parent": {"cref": "#/groups/1"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "list_item", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 316.06580315, "t": 554.0447247988577, "r": 426.59142125460505, "b": 540.8986020255827, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 23]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/86", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 315.6727835000001, "t": 540.4950473488577, "r": 352.6346623015401, "b": 527.3489245755827, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 7]}]}], "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.2 MedQA", "Prompt with Question"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 9293128959098327548, "filename": "rec_003258_acl.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:31:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 31, "text": "D\nTable 2: Prompt example with a question and expected response from MedQA.\nsions, one of which is an English version sourced from the United States Medical License Exams. While MMLU's professional medicine subject also includes questions from USMLE practice examinations, MedQA's English version sets itself apart by incorporating questions drawn from both real exams and mock tests for USMLE. 1,273 USMLEstyle questions are provided as the test dataset to benchmark the model's ability to answer medical questions at the professional level. Each question is accompanied by four or five answer choices and corresponding relevant document collections, intended to help models in generating accurate responses.", "contextualized_text": "3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation\n3.2.2 MedQA\nExpected Response:\nD\nTable 2: Prompt example with a question and expected response from MedQA.\nsions, one of which is an English version sourced from the United States Medical License Exams. While MMLU's professional medicine subject also includes questions from USMLE practice examinations, MedQA's English version sets itself apart by incorporating questions drawn from both real exams and mock tests for USMLE. 1,273 USMLEstyle questions are provided as the test dataset to benchmark the model's ability to answer medical questions at the professional level. Each question is accompanied by four or five answer choices and corresponding relevant document collections, intended to help models in generating accurate responses.", "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.2 MedQA", "Expected Response:"], "pages": [5], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/88", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 412.47262325, "t": 526.5463499488575, "r": 420.34938726851004, "b": 513.4002271755825, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 1]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/89", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 305.8352916500001, "t": 502.8766005205576, "r": 524.4258937734576, "b": 478.9154695239076, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 73]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/90", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 305.6312814500001, "t": 453.4536954988576, "r": 526.3308448104472, "b": 264.1587657255825, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 633]}]}], "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.2 MedQA", "Expected Response:"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 9293128959098327548, "filename": "rec_003258_acl.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:32:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 32, "text": "MedMCQA (Pal et al., 2022) is a benchmark with questions sourced from postgraduate-level Indian medical school entrance exams (AIIMS and NEET PG). Covering a breadth of medical specialties, the dataset has questions about 2,400 healthcare topics and 21 subjects within the medical domain. 4,183 MCQ, each offering four answer choices, are provided for evaluation.", "contextualized_text": "3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation\n3.2.3 MedMCQA\nMedMCQA (Pal et al., 2022) is a benchmark with questions sourced from postgraduate-level Indian medical school entrance exams (AIIMS and NEET PG). Covering a breadth of medical specialties, the dataset has questions about 2,400 healthcare topics and 21 subjects within the medical domain. 4,183 MCQ, each offering four answer choices, are provided for evaluation.", "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.3 MedMCQA"], "pages": [5], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/92", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 305.76228800000007, "t": 240.66105639885745, "r": 526.3318266785377, "b": 132.66519137558248, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 363]}]}], "headings": ["3.2 Medical LLM Evaluation", "3.2.3 MedMCQA"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 9293128959098327548, "filename": "rec_003258_acl.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/docling_uncertain_problem_retry_no_vlm_2026-07-08/chunks/rec_003258_acl.jsonl:33:{"candidate_id": "rec_003258_acl", "chunk_index": 33, "text": "The preliminary results in Table 3 for the medical large language training provide several notable trends. Firstly, there is a clear trend between model size and performance, with larger models consistently achieving higher accuracy scores across all three benchmark datasets. For instance, the LLaMA-2 model, particularly in its larger 70billion-parameter model, shows superior performance compared to smaller models. This underscores the importance of model scale in capturing the complexity of medical language and achieving better task performance. However, due to the constraints of the scarce computational resources at the hospital, smaller models with adequate performance can be preferred.\n", "contextualized_text": "3.3 Evaluation Results\nThe preliminary results in Table 3 for the medical large language training provide several notable trends. Firstly, there is a clear trend between model size and performance, with larger models consistently achieving higher accuracy scores across all three benchmark datasets. For instance, the LLaMA-2 model, particularly in its larger 70billion-parameter model, shows superior performance compared to smaller models. This underscores the importance of model scale in capturing the complexity of medical language and achieving better task performance. However, due to the constraints of the scarce computational resources at the hospital, smaller models with adequate performance can be preferred.\n", "headings": ["3.3 Evaluation Results"], "pages": [5, 6], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/94", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 5, "bbox": {"l": 305.80629020000003, "t": 106.22133474885754, "r": 526.2376403544569, "