ey of Multimodal Large Language Models in Biomedical Engineering and Healthcare', so this is a review paper rather than a primary model contribution.","evidence_snippet":"\"A Survey of Multimodal Large Language Models in Biomedical Engineering and Healthcare\""},{"record_id":"rec_003264","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a new foundational agent for multi-omics interpretation with explicit reasoning and latent embeddings, but it does not describe a text or language component. It is therefore outside the generative text-bio scope.","evidence_snippet":"\"We introduce BiOmics, a foundational agent that synthesizes multi-omics data\"; \"explicit reasoning space\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0165.prompt.txt:52:[{"record_id":"rec_003255","title":"Challenges in AI-driven biomedical multimodal data fusion and analysis","abstract":"Abstract\n                  The rapid development of biological and medical examination methods has vastly expanded personal biomedical information, including molecular, cellular, image, and electronic health record datasets. Integrating this wealth of information enables precise disease diagnosis, biomarker identification, and treatment design in clinical settings. Artificial intelligence (AI) techniques, particularly deep learning models, have been extensively employed in biomedical applications, demonstrating increased precision, efficiency, and generalization. The success of the large language and vision models further significantly extends their biomedical applications. However, challenges remain in learning these multimodal biomedical datasets, such as data privacy, fusion, and model interpretation. In this review, we provide a comprehensive overview of various biomedical data modalities, multimodal representation learning methods, and the applications of AI in biomedical data integrative analysis. Additionally, we discuss the challenges in applying these deep learning methods and how to better integrate them into biomedical scenarios. We then propose future directions for adapting deep learning methods with model pretraining and knowledge integration to advance biomedical research and benefit their clinical applications.","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"Genomics …","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003255","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is explicitly a review of biomedical multimodal data fusion and analysis. It mentions large language and vision models, but the abstract does not establish a clear text-bio candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"“In this review, we provide a comprehensive overview” and “the success of the large language and vision models”"},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003255","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of AI-driven biomedical multimodal data fusion and analysis. It discusses deep learning and large language and vision models generally, but does not describe a specific generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this review, we provide a comprehensive overview\"; \"the success of the large language and vision models\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"review_editorial","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_003256","title":"Large language models for bioinformatics","abstract":"LLMs are a type of foundation model trained on vast datasets to  omics data (eg, genomics,  transcriptomics, proteomics) and  Recent advances in multi-modal LLM architecture have","doi":"","year":"2026","venue":"Quantitative …","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003256","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title and fragment suggest bioinformatics-focused LLM content, but the abstract is too truncated to determine whether this is a primary model paper or a review. The text-bio bridge is not clearly stated.","evidence_snippet":"“Large language models for bioinformatics” and “Recent advances in multi-modal LLM architecture”"},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003256","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is about large language models in bioinformatics as a general topic, not a new candidate model. The foundation-model statement is definitional rather than evidence for a specific pretrained model.","evidence_snippet":"\"LLMs are a type of foundation model trained on vast datasets\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"review_editorial","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_003257","title":"LLMAgent4Bio: LLM Agents for Biological Intelligence Across Genomics, Proteomics, Spatial Biology, and Biomedicine","abstract":"Abstract\n                Large language models are evolving from passive predictors into agentic systems capable of planning, tool use, and multimodal reasoning. This shift is especially consequential for biology, where complex, noisy, and multi-scale data require adaptive and integrative computational strategies. In this review, we provide the first systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics, molecular biology, imaging, biomedical analysis, and automated bioinformatics workflows. We analyze more than fifty emerging systems and organize them within a unifying framework that characterizes agentic traits such as autonomous decision-making, external tool invocation, memory, and self-correction. Across domains, agentic LLMs show early promise in enabling multi-step analysis, linking heterogeneous evidence, and supporting exploratory scientific tasks. At the same time, our comparative assessment highlights consistent challenges, including unstable reasoning, limited biological grounding, retrieval misalignment, and barriers to reproducibility and biosafety. We conclude by outlining opportunities for trustworthy and collaborative biological agents, including multimodal integration, closedloop experimental design, and robust evaluation practices. This survey aims to clarify the emerging landscape and chart a path toward reliable agentic systems for biological discovery.","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"NA","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003257","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Abstract explicitly says 'In this review' and describes a 'systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics, molecular biology, imaging, biomedical analysis'. Biology and LLMs are both central.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this review, we provide the first systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics...\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003257","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a systematic review of LLM-based agents, not a primary model paper. It summarizes existing systems across biology rather than presenting a new generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"we provide the first systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"review_editorial","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present