ationale":"The abstract describes embedding-based deep learning for multimodal oncology data integration, which is predictive rather than generative. It does not provide evidence of a foundation-model-style generative architecture.","evidence_snippet":"\"Embedding-Based Deep Learning Frameworks for Multimodal Oncology Data Integration\""},{"record_id":"rec_003261","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly identifies the work as a survey of biomedical data analysis with LLMs. No new generative model is described.","evidence_snippet":"\"The large language models on biomedical data analysis: a survey\""},{"record_id":"rec_003262","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a comprehensive review of LLM applications in bioinformatics, not a primary model description. The abstract discusses applications and challenges rather than a specific generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This comprehensive review systematically examines the development and applications of LLMs in bioinformatics\""},{"record_id":"rec_003263","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title states that this is a survey of multimodal LLMs in biomedical engineering and healthcare. That makes it a review rather than a primary generative model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"A Survey of Multimodal Large Language Models in Biomedical Engineering and Healthcare\""},{"record_id":"rec_003264","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"BiOmics is presented as a foundational agent with cross-scale interpretive capability, but the abstract centers on retrieving, reasoning, and predicting rather than a clearly generative architecture. It does suggest broad applicability across tasks, which is foundation-like evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"Retrieving-Reasoning-Predicting\" and \"reference-free cell annotation\" / \"drug repurposing candidates\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0098.stderr.log:1848:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0350.stderr.log:1529:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0408.stderr.log:313:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_003257","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Abstract explicitly says 'In this review' and describes a 'systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics, molecular biology, imaging, biomedical analysis'. Biology and LLMs are both central.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this review, we provide the first systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics...\""},{"record_id":"rec_003258","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title links knowledge graphs and protein structures to large language models, but the abstract is fragmentary and reads like a proposal ('Here I propose to work on...'). It is not clear whether this is a completed primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"Foundation model for biomedical graphs: Integrating knowledge graphs and protein structures to large language models\"; \"Here I propose to work on...\""},{"record_id":"rec_003259","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract tie LLMs to biological sequence analysis, but the abstract fragment is too incomplete to confirm whether this is a primary study, review, or resource paper. The biological and language components are still evident.","evidence_snippet":"\"Large language models for biological sequence analysis in infectious disease research\""},{"record_id":"rec_003260","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is about multimodal oncology data integration and foundation-model-driven dataset generation, but it does not describe a substantive text or language component. That makes it outside the text-bio scope.","evidence_snippet":"\"Embedding-Based Deep Learning Frameworks for Multimodal Oncology Data Integration\"; \"foundation model-driven approach to generating multimodal oncology datasets\""},{"record_id":"rec_003261","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title explicitly says 'a survey' and the abstract says it 'comprehensively reviews' LLM applications in biomedical data analysis. This is a review rather than a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"The large language models on biomedical data analysis: a survey\"; \"This comprehensive review\""},{"record_id":"rec_003262","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract repeatedly frames the paper as a comprehensive review of LLMs in bioinformatics and 'systematically summarize[s] the current research status'. That is clearly review/editorial.","evidence_snippet":"\"This comprehensive review systematically examines...\""},{"record_id":"rec_003263","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title says 'A Survey of Multimodal Large Language Models in Biomedical Engineering and Healthcare', so this is a review paper rather than a primary model contribution.","evidence_snippet":"\"A Survey of Multimodal Large Language Models in Biomedical Engineering and Healthcare\""},{"record_id":"rec_003264","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a new foundational agent for multi-omics interpretation with explicit reasoning and latent embeddings, but it does not describe a text or language component. It is therefore outside the generative text-bio scope.","evidence_snippet":"\"We introduce BiOmics, a foundational agent that synthesizes multi-omics data\"; \"explicit reasoning space\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0282.stderr.log:850:./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0408.prompt.txt:51:[{"record_id":"rec_003257","title":"LLMAgent4Bio: LLM Agents for Biological Intelligence Across Genomics, Proteomics, Spatial Biology, and Biomedicine","abstract":"Abstract\n                Large language models are evolving from passive predictors into agentic systems capable of planning, tool use, and multimodal reasoning. This shift is especially consequential for biology, where complex, noisy, and multi-scale data require adaptive and integrative computational strategies. In this review, we provide the first systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics, molecular biology, imaging, biomedical analysis, and automated bioinformatics workflows. We analyze more than fifty emerging systems and organize them within a unifying framework that characterizes agentic traits such as autonomous decision-making, external tool invocation, memory, and self-correction. Across domains, agentic LLMs show early promise in enabling multi-step analysis, linking heterogeneous evidence, and supporting exploratory scientific tasks. At the same time, our comparative assessment highlights consistent challenges, including unstable reasoning, limited biological grounding, retrieval misalignment, and barriers to reproducibility and biosafety. We conclude by outlining opportunities for trustworthy and collaborative biological agents, including multimodal integration, closedloop experimental design, and robust evaluation practices. This survey aims to clarify the emerging landscape and chart a path toward reliable agentic systems for biological discovery.","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"NA","sources":["google_scholar"]},{"record_id":"rec_003258","title":"Foundation model for biomedical graphs: Integrating knowledge graphs and protein structures to large language models","abstract":", multimodal LLM in the biomedical domain is primarily limited to images, text, and/or sequence  data. Here I propose to work on multimodal LLM  -art foundation model with genetics and","doi":"","year":"2024","venue":"Proceedings of the 62nd Annual Meeting of the …","sources":["google_scholar"]},{"record_id":"rec_003259","title":"Large language models for biological sequence analysis in infectious disease research","abstract":"models, genomic language models, and multimodal models,  the emergence of computational,  LLM-based approaches for  foundation model and benchmark for multi species genomes","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"Biosafety and Health","sources":["google_scholar"]},{"record_id":"rec_003260","title":"Embedding-Based Deep Learning Frameworks for Multimodal Oncology Data Integration","abstract":"our foundation model-driven approach to generating multimodal oncology datasets. We show   We discuss the challenges and limitations of implementing multimodal data-fusion models","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"NA","sources":["google_scholar"]},{"record_id":"rec_003261","title":"The large language models on biomedical data analysis: a survey","abstract":"of LLMs in genomics, proteomics, transcriptomics, single-cell  BERT-based LLM that uses a  multi-modal self-supervised pre foundation model and benchmark for multi-species genome.","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"IEEE Journal of …","sources":["google_scholar"]},{"record_id":"rec_003262","title":"Bridging artificial intelligence and biological sciences: a comprehensive review of large language models in bioinformatics","abstract":"Abstract\n               Large language models (LLMs), representing a breakthrough advancement in artificial intelligence, have demonstrated substantial application value and development potential in bioinformatics research, particularly showing significant progress in the processing and analysis of complex biological data. This comprehensive review systematically examines the development and applications of LLMs in bioinformatics, with particular emphasis on their advancements in protein and nucleic acid structure prediction, omics analysis, drug design and screening, and biomedical literature mining. This work highlights the distinctive capabilities of LLMs in end-to-end learning and knowledge transfer paradigms. Additionally, this paper thoroughly discusses the major challenges confronting LLMs in current applications, including key issues such as model interpretability and data bias. Furthermore, this review comprehensively explores the potential of LLMs in cross-modal learning and interdisciplinary development. In conclusion, this paper aims to systematically summarize the current research status of LLMs in bioinformatics, objectively evaluate their advantages and limitations, and provide insights and recommendations for future research directions, thereby positioning LLMs as essential tools in bioinformatics research and fostering innovative developments in the biomedical field.","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"Briefings in …","sources":["google_scholar"]},{"record_id":"rec_003263","title":"A Survey of Multimodal Large Language Models in Biomedical Engineering and Healthcare","abstract":"data are inherently multimodal: imaging, waveforms, genomics,  fine-tunes the Otter  foundation model to generate volumetric CT  Xu, “Do we really need a multimodal llm decoder?","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"Authorea …","sources":["google_scholar"]},{"record_id":"rec_003264","title":"BiOmics: A Foundational Agent for Grounded and Autonomous Multi-omics Interpretation","abstract":"Abstract\n                While AI has automated bioinformatic workflows, biological interpretation remains fragmented and often disconnected from mechanistic insights. Existing AI is bifurcated between statistical “black-box” models that lack logical grounding and simple agents restricted to shallow knowledge retrieval. To bridge this divide, we introduce BiOmics, a foundational agent that synthesizes multi-omics data with adaptive knowledge for biological interpretation. BiOmics introduces a novel dual-track architecture comprising a harmonized explicit reasoning space for grounded logic and a unified latent embedding space for high-dimensional association mapping. This architecture enables a transformative “Retrieving-Reasoning-Predicting” paradigm for purposeful, cross-scale inference traversing the biological hierarchy, from molecular variants to disease phenotypes. Empirical evaluations demonstrate that BiOmics surpasses state-of-the-art AI agents and specialized algorithms, markedly augmenting the granularity and depth of biological insights. Specifically, BiOmics exhibits unique superiority in uncovering indirect pathogenic variants, achieving reference-free cell annotation, and prioritizing drug repurposing candidates tailored to specific datasets. BiOmics further enriches the interpretive landscape of biological entities, leveraging its reasoning-grounded knowledge graph to uncover deep functional contexts. Ultimately, BiOmics provides a versatile engineering foundation to transition AI for Science from descriptive “data fitting” to autonomous, knowledge-driven interpretation.","doi":"","year":"2026","venue":"bioRxiv","sources":["google_scholar"]}]
