 text-bio bridge is not clearly stated.","evidence_snippet":"“Large language models for bioinformatics” and “Recent advances in multi-modal LLM architecture”"},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003256","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is about large language models in bioinformatics as a general topic, not a new candidate model. The foundation-model statement is definitional rather than evidence for a specific pretrained model.","evidence_snippet":"\"LLMs are a type of foundation model trained on vast datasets\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"review_editorial","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_003257","title":"LLMAgent4Bio: LLM Agents for Biological Intelligence Across Genomics, Proteomics, Spatial Biology, and Biomedicine","abstract":"Abstract\n                Large language models are evolving from passive predictors into agentic systems capable of planning, tool use, and multimodal reasoning. This shift is especially consequential for biology, where complex, noisy, and multi-scale data require adaptive and integrative computational strategies. In this review, we provide the first systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics, molecular biology, imaging, biomedical analysis, and automated bioinformatics workflows. We analyze more than fifty emerging systems and organize them within a unifying framework that characterizes agentic traits such as autonomous decision-making, external tool invocation, memory, and self-correction. Across domains, agentic LLMs show early promise in enabling multi-step analysis, linking heterogeneous evidence, and supporting exploratory scientific tasks. At the same time, our comparative assessment highlights consistent challenges, including unstable reasoning, limited biological grounding, retrieval misalignment, and barriers to reproducibility and biosafety. We conclude by outlining opportunities for trustworthy and collaborative biological agents, including multimodal integration, closedloop experimental design, and robust evaluation practices. This survey aims to clarify the emerging landscape and chart a path toward reliable agentic systems for biological discovery.","doi":"","year":"2025","venue":"NA","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003257","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Abstract explicitly says 'In this review' and describes a 'systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics, molecular biology, imaging, biomedical analysis'. Biology and LLMs are both central.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this review, we provide the first systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents across genomics...\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003257","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a systematic review of LLM-based agents, not a primary model paper. It summarizes existing systems across biology rather than presenting a new generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"we provide the first systematic synthesis of LLM-based agents\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"review_editorial","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present